# Line endings.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (19 September 2026). A `.mjs` script checked out with
# CRLF line endings CANNOT BE IMPORTED BY VITEST: the suite fails to collect the
# importing test with "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token", pointing at no
# line and no file. esbuild and tsc both parse the same file happily, so nothing
# else in the toolchain disagrees, which makes it very hard to attribute.
#
# It cost an hour after a routine merge normalised line endings and took
# scripts/check-route-conflicts.mjs from LF to CRLF. Seven scripts under
# scripts/ are imported directly by tests, so any of them can trip this, and it
# recurs on any checkout that renormalises.
#
# Scoped deliberately to the extensions that have actually broken rather than a
# blanket `* text=auto`, which would renormalise the whole repository in one
# commit and bury everything else in the diff.
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.cjs text eol=lf
